% Bus fixture: ONE person of the gossip world (the three-world
% wiring of domains/ceptre/gossip/gossip.llp, metis-catalog). The social
% graph is NOT here: `follows` became DRIVER wiring — who hears
% whose posts is bus policy on the blackboard. The world only knows
% how to hear, learn and repost; same once-token discipline as the
% single-world port.
% Attribution: re-expresses interactive-lp's gossip.cep (Chris Martens, ACSL v1.4).
catalog gossip_node 1.
provenance hand "bus fixture: one gossip person; the graph is the wiring" "2026-10-03".
layers (dyn).
stages (talk).
type message {m1 m2 m3}.
namespace st produce (dyn).
pred heard(message) : st.
pred unheard(message) : st.
pred knows(message) : st.
pred not_posted(message) : st.
pred posted(message) : st.
stage talk {
  %% a first hearing: the message becomes known and repostable.
  hear [dyn] : heard(M) * unheard(M) -o knows(M) * not_posted(M).
  %% a known, unposted message goes out.
  post [dyn] : $knows(M) * not_posted(M) -o posted(M).
}
#steps 10
